# Theme Color Modes

Figma (EISCO Main variables) is the **structure** SSOT. **01.01 Theme/Primitives** ≈ stock Tailwind (spacing / text / rounded) — use `--spacing()` / default theme; do not re-declare every `--spacing-8`. Figma half-steps (`0,5`, `9xl-1`, `12rem`) are **cleanup**, not Liquid classes — do not invent them.

**Everything from `01.02 Theme/Brand` onward is customized.** Discover exact names from this repo’s `_styles/` (and Figma when scaffolding tokens). Names below are **illustrative**.

## Two axes (keep them separate)

### 1. Brand vertical → `<html>` (`01.02 Theme/Brand`)

Figma modes: `education` | `industrial`.

Runtime intent: a **single class on `<html>`** that rebinds Brand-dependent CSS variables (accent / neutral ramps, fonts, radii) so the whole tree flips:

```liquid
<html class="brand-educational">
<!-- or -->
<html class="brand-industrial">
```

Accept either `brand-educational` / `brand-education` (and the industrial pair) — **discover the exact class** from `_styles/` / `layout/theme.liquid` / `_layout/theme.liquid`. Do not put the brand class on the section. Do not restyle children with Brand ramps.

### 2. Section tone → section root (`02.02 Base/Colors`)

Six tones: `primary` | `secondary` | `muted` | `accent` | `contrast` | `elevated`.

Put the matching mode class on the **section root** (often `color-schema-*`). New Figma-driven themes use this set — a single `accent` tone, **not** `accent-1` / `accent-2` / `accent-3`.

Children use **only semantic roles**. The tone remaps those tokens.

**Older `_styles/`:** some themes still ship `color-schema-accent-1|2|3` and omit `elevated`. Use grep. Do not invent `color-schema-elevated` or treat accent-1/2/3 as the Figma SSOT.

## Semantic roles (`02.02 Base/Colors`)

When present in `_styles/`, Liquid uses:

- **bg:** `surface` | `subtle` | `emphasis` | `accent` | `accent-sec`
- **text:** `primary` | `secondary` | `accent` | `on-accent` | `on-accent-sec`
- **border:** `primary` | `secondary` | `tertiary` | `accent` | `on-accent` | `on-accent-sec`

`02.03 Base/Alphacolors` (`0-*` overlays) is **legacy** — not the primary API.

If `_styles/` is missing a Figma role (`text-accent`, `bg-accent-sec`, `border-tertiary`, `border-accent`, `elevated`), do **not** invent it or fall back to hex. Closest shipped semantic utility, or a theme `_styles` PR.

Brand ramps (`color/neutral/*`, `color/accent/*`, `color/brand/*`) are CSS-only — never Liquid classes.

## Overridden Tailwind utilities (`02.01 Base/Sizes`)

Figma `max-width/sm|base|lg|xl|2xl` (modes `lg` | `md` | `default`) aliases into `spacing/*` and may **redefine stock Tailwind** (`max-w-sm`, etc.) via `@theme` / `@utility max-w-*` plus breakpoint remaps.

**Do not assume stock Tailwind values** for any utility listed in `_styles/02_base/*sizes*`. Grep theme tokens first. Same pattern may apply to `px` / `py` / `gap` / `height` / `icon` / `text-size`. Layout density modes map to `md:` / `lg:` — never hard `px`.

## Components → atoms (`03.01` / `03.02`)

`03.01 Components/Sizes` (button / input × `lg` | `base` | `sm`) and `03.02 Components/Colors` (`primary` | `secondary`, including state opacities) are **not** flat section tokens. They map to **atom CSS** (`a--button`, inputs) composed from Base semantic tokens.

Build UI with existing atom classes / data attributes (`{% render 'a--button', ... %}`). Do **not** invent `button/height` utilities. If atoms do not implement the Figma matrix yet, that is a theme `_styles` gap — do not fake with hex.

## Mode first

1. Grep `_styles/` (and `theme.liquid`) for brand class, `@utility` / `color-schema-*`, `@theme` size overrides, semantic roles, atoms.
2. Set **brand** on `<html>` when the theme has that axis.
3. Set **tone** on the section root.
4. Children: semantic roles only. Buttons/inputs: atoms, not one-off utilities.

```bash
rg -n "@utility|color-schema|brand-educat|brand-industrial|max-w-|--background-color|--text-color|--border-color|@theme|elevated" _styles/ layout/ _layout/
```

Then read `figma-design-system.mdc` and `tailwindcss-rules.mdc`.

## Forbidden

- Arbitrary hex / rgb: `text-[#d1d1d1]`, `bg-[#fff]`
- Inventing tokens, Figma half-steps, or `button/height`-style utilities
- Liquid-built class names: `text-{{ color }}`
- Brand ramps or primitive scales as Liquid classes
- Assuming stock Tailwind `max-w-*` / spacing when `_styles/02_base/*sizes*` overrides them
- Teaching `accent-1|2|3` as the Figma tone list
- Putting brand vertical on the section instead of `<html>`

## Illustrative only

```liquid
<html class="brand-educational">
  …
  <section class="color-schema-muted">
    <div class="bg-surface text-primary border-secondary">
      <h2 class="text-primary">…</h2>
      <p class="text-secondary">…</p>
      {% render 'a--button', variant: 'primary', size: 'base' %}
    </div>
  </section>
```

Replace every class / param with what this theme’s `_styles/` and atoms actually define.
